1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:06,784
Lunchtime has arrived—the meal is ready, but Ababa and
Ene's grandson Abush is nowhere nearby.

2
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:12,234
Abush went to the neighboring village to play—he even
forgot that lunchtime had arrived.

3
00:00:12,242 --> 00:00:18,466
Ababa returned from work; after a tiring day, once the
house settled, he sat down to eat lunch.

4
00:00:18,467 --> 00:00:24,883
Ababa asked, 'Where is Abush?' So Ababa wouldn't get
upset, Ene said, 'He is right around here.'

5
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:30,716
Inside, however, she hurried—she rushed to the other
village to bring Abush before Ababa noticed.

6
00:00:30,708 --> 00:00:37,196
When she found Abush, she put him on her back and said, 'I
told Ababa you're right here—let's go quickly.'

7
00:00:37,183 --> 00:00:42,783
Once seated on her back, Abush laughed and
smilingly said, 'Ene, you are a leopard!'

8
00:00:42,783 --> 00:00:48,551
Ene's fast dash and Abush's joke became an
unforgettable memory inside the family.

9
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:54,726
After that, whenever Ene tells this story to the family,
everyone shares laughs and laughs again.

10
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:56,949
Ene, you are a leopard!
